  "body": "Add `mindensity` and `maxdensity` content attributes (reflected as `minDensity` and `maxDensity` on `HTMLImageElement` and `HTMLSourceElement`) to clamp the target pixel density (`devicePixelRatio`) used when selecting an image source from a source set.\n\nStacked on #13183:\n\n- **Content and IDL attributes**: Adds `mindensity` and `maxdensity` to `<img>` and `<source>` (when inside `<picture>`), reflected as `minDensity` and `maxDensity` (`DOMString`). Values are parsed using the rules for parsing floating-point number values; non-positive values and parse errors are ignored.\n- **Per-attribute fallback in `<picture>`**: When a `<source>` element is selected in `<picture>`, each of `mindensity` and `maxdensity` falls back independently to the corresponding attribute on the `<img>` element if not present on `<source>`.\n- **Target density clamping**: In *select an image source from a source set*, `targetDensity` starts at `devicePixelRatio`, is clamped to `maximum density` (`min(targetDensity, maxDensity)`), and then to `minimum density` (`max(targetDensity, minDensity)`), so `mindensity` takes precedence if `mindensity > maxdensity` (matching CSS `min`/`max` clamping).\n- **Relevant mutations**: Setting, changing, or removing `mindensity` or `maxdensity` on `<img>` or a preceding sibling `<source>` in `<picture>` triggers *update the image data*.\n\nFixes #4421.\nFixes #13069.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64738\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n\n### :boom: Error: Wattsi server error :boom: ###\n\n[PR Preview](https://github.com/specinfra/pr-preview#pr-preview) failed to build. _(Last tried on Nov 25, 2026, 11:24 AM UTC)_.\n\n<details>\n<summary>More</summary>\n\n\nPR Preview relies on a number of web services to run. There seems to be an issue with the following one:\n\n:rotating_light: [Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server) - Wattsi Server is the web service used to build the WHATWG HTML spec.\n\n:link: [Related URL](https://build.whatwg.org/wattsi)\n\n**Error output:**\n\n```\n      <!DOCTYPE html>\n      <html>\n      <head>\n          <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n          <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">\n          <style>body,html{height:100%;margin:0}body{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-direction:column;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility}p{text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Segoe UI,Roboto,Oxygen,Ubuntu,Cantarell,Fira Sans,Droid Sans,Helvetica Neue,sans-serif;color:#000;font-size:14px;margin-top:-50px}p.code{font-size:24px;font-weight:500;border-bottom:1px solid #e0e1e2;padding:0 20px 15px}p.text{margin:0}a,a:visited{color:#aaa}</style>\n      </head>\n      <body>\n      <p class=\"code\">\n        Error code: 503      </p>\n      <p class=\"text\">\n        Well, This is unexpected. An Error has occurred, and we are working to fix the problem! We will be up and running shortly. Try refreshing the page or try again in a few minutes.\n      </p>\n        <div style=\"display:none;\">\n          <h1>\n    upstream_reset_before_response_started{connection_termination} (503 UC)      </h1>\n          <p data-translate=\"connection_timed_out\">App Platform failed to forward this request to the application.</p>\n      </div>\n      </body>\n      </html>\n    \n```\n\n_This seems to be an issue with the [Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server) service. PR Preview doesn't manage this service and so has no control over it. If you've identified an issue with it, you can [report the issue to the maintainers of Wattsi Server](https://github.com/domenic/wattsi-server/issues/new) directly. Please be courteous. Thank you!_\n\n_If you don't have enough information above to solve the error by yourself or if the issue doesn't seem related to Wattsi Server, you can [file an issue with PR Preview](https://github.com/specinfra/pr-preview/issues/new?title=Unidentified%20Error&body=See%20whatwg/html%2313192.)._\n\n</details>\n",
